<title>FINLAND: CASTRUM SOLD J.TALLBERG SHARES.</title>
<headline>CASTRUM SOLD J.TALLBERG SHARES.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Real estate investment company Castrum Oy said in a statement on Monday its Vedex Oy subsidiary had sold 556,032 B-shares in real estate company Julius Tallberg Kiinteistot Oy, 15.7 percent of shares and 3.9 percent of votes.</p>
<p>&quot;The earnings impact for the Castrum group is an 11.6 million marKka gain,&quot; Castrum said.</p>
<p>The buyers had been domestic and international investors. The transaction had been handled by FIM Pankkiiriliike, it said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 9 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
